<p>
=86 <strong>N.B.</strong> : When benchmarking, beware the powersavings=20
mode! Mpiram seems to get its timing from the initial frequency of the=20
CPU, so starting from a CPU in a low-frequency power savings mode and=20
using an older linux kernel will give timing errors of a factor of 2 or=20
so. When timing, it may be better to get the CPU's spun up to maximum=20
somehow before starting mpiram.
</p><p>
